 ### Parameters
-*   $f_{vn}$: Known CT number (scalar value) for tissue type $n$. Ordered $f_{v1} < f_{v2} < \dots < f_{vN}$ [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   $\alpha_{vn}$: Target opacity assigned to tissue type $n$ at $f_{vn}$ [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   $N$: Number of tissue types, $N \ge 1$ [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+*   $F_{vn}$: Known CT number (scalar value) for tissue type $n$, $n=1 \dots N$, $N \ge 1$, ordered $F_{v1} < F_{v2} < \dots < F_{vN}$ [S2, unofficial].
+*   $\alpha_{vn}$: Target opacity assigned to tissue type $n$ at $F_{vn}$ [S2, unofficial].
+*   $K$: Number of sample locations along each ray [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Adjacency Violation:** If non-adjacent tissue types touch (e.g., $|n-m| > 1$), voxels at boundaries cannot be unambiguously classified [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. Solution: Interactive clipping to isolate subsets meeting criteria [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Thin Features:** Binary thresholds may miss thin features of tissue type B if their voxel values are less than $f_{vB}$. This method maps all voxels to non-zero opacity, rendering thin regions as faint wisps [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Gradient Artifacts:** CT scanners have anisotropic spatial sensitivity, causing striping. Patient motion also causes striping because shading depends on gradient orientation; misalignments between adjacent slices disrupt this [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Constant Transition Thickness:** The thickness of the transition region around isosurface contours remains constant only if the local gradient magnitude is constant within a radius of $r$ voxels around each point on the surface [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Rotation Shading:** Fixing colors and opacities while rotating causes light sources to appear to travel with the data, creating incorrect highlights [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Adjacency Violation:** If tissue types do not touch only adjacent types in the ordered list, voxels at boundaries cannot be unambiguously classified [S1, S2, unofficial]. Solution: Interactive clipping to isolate subsets meeting criteria [S1, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Thin Features:** Binary thresholds may miss thin features or detect noise. This method maps all voxels to non-zero opacity, rendering thin regions as faint wisps [S1, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Gradient Dependence:** Shading and opacity scaling depend on gradient orientation. Misalignments between adjacent slices (e.g., from patient motion or CT scanner anisotropy) cause striping artifacts [S1, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Constant Gradient Assumption:** The thickness of the transition region around isosurface contours remains constant only if the local gradient magnitude is constant within a radius of $r$ voxels around the surface [S1, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Rotation Artifacts:** Fixing colors and opacities while rotating the view causes light sources to appear to travel with the data, creating incorrect highlights [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
 
 ### Time and Memory Complexity
-*   **Opacity Computation:** $O(V)$ where $V$ is the number of voxels. If gradient magnitudes are pre-stored, mapping to opacity requires one lookup table reference per voxel [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Ray Tracing/Compositing:** For a square image of $n$ pixels with $K$ samples per ray and orthographic projection: $3Kn^2$ additions, $2Kn^2$ tri-linear interpolations, and $Kn^2$ linear interpolations [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Opacity Computation:** One lookup table reference per voxel if gradient magnitudes are pre-stored. New lookup table generation is required if classification parameters change [S1, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Ray Tracing/Compositing:** For a square image of $n$ pixels with $K$ samples per ray, the cost is $3Kn^2$ additions, $2Kn^2$ tri-linear interpolations, and $Kn^2$ linear interpolations [S1, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Memory:** Requires storage for the volume data and optionally the pre-computed gradient magnitude grid [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
 ### Measured Performance
